 {"id": "QA-CONSOLE-3", "title": "[P2] the console tools in tools/console/ are not wired to any runner, so nothing runs them automatically", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": "2", "depends_on": ["QA-CONSOLE-2"], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Bane asked for the extra tools to live in the project directory and for the work to be on the board; both are done, and this is the follow-on. tools/console/ now holds test_controls.py, test_pass.py, test_auto_vision.py, bench_vision_accuracy.py, bench_equipped.py and the measured vision prompt. Nothing invokes them: they pass only when a human remembers to run them, which is exactly how the toggle bug survived until Bane asked about it directly. Criteria: a runner (make target or small script) that starts the console if it is down, runs test_controls.py and test_pass.py against it, fails loudly on any non-200 or any toggle that ignores its input, and is reachable from the QA lane or a cron entry so the console stops depending on my memory. Note the movement buttons cannot be covered by an unattended runner: pressing them changes game state and needs explicit approval, so the runner must skip them explicitly rather than silently pass them.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/ai-plays-poke-QA-CONSOLE-3", "branch": "wt/QA-CONSOLE-3", "worker_status": "complete", "worker_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "worker_provider": "openai-codex", "commit_hash": "7c9ea78", "guard_result": "tier1 FAIL = secrets/tests cmd-timeout (known env artifact, no leak); tier2 PASS verdict 15ed908a", "ci_result": "GREEN", "completed_at": "2026-10-02T13:45:00Z", "foreman_note": "Tick ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-02-15-06-27: worker commit 7c9ea78 verified on main (Makefile run-qa target + tools/console/run_qa.py); prior tick closed bookkeeping only."}
